This product is a standalone companion to dorabot and ships no dorabot code as a
dependency. It does, however, contain work derived from dorabot, which is
likewise MIT licensed:

    dorabot
    https://github.com/suitedaces/dorabot
    Copyright (c) suitedaces
    MIT License

Specifically, the conversation reconstruction logic in
packages/protocol/src/stream.ts is a port of the stream handling in dorabot's
desktop renderer (desktop/src/hooks/useGateway.ts), namely applyStreamEvent,
appendToolOutputDelta, sessionMessagesToChatItems and cleanToolName.

That logic is subtle in ways that are not obvious from reading it, and getting it
wrong produces conversations that silently lose text or leave tool spinners
running forever. It is reproduced faithfully rather than reinvented, with the
non-obvious behaviours documented in comments at the top of the file.

The wire protocol types in packages/protocol/src/gateway.ts describe dorabot's
gateway as observed at version 0.3.2. They were derived from the case arms of its
RPC switch rather than from its exported type unions, which are out of date
relative to the implementation.
